/-
This module defines `OptimizationType` and `OracleLevel` (as `Fin 6`), and the function `optRequiredLevel`. It then proves `T1_14_opt_safety_monotone`, which states that if an optimization O₁ requires a lower or equal oracle level than O₂, and the achieved level meets O₂'s requirement, then it also meets O₁'s requirement. This is proven using the transitivity of the `≤` relation on `OracleLevel`.
-/

import Mathlib

set_option linter.mathlibStandardSet false

open scoped BigOperators
